1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,341
This is VOID.

2
00:00:01,391 --> 00:00:07,824
Give an AI agent real on-chain power, with a guarantee it can never leave your rules.

3
00:00:07,874 --> 00:00:10,646
A smart contract checks every action.

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:15,302
Every action passes five gates, in a fixed order:

5
00:00:15,352 --> 00:00:20,362
expiry, spend cap, whitelist, transaction count, rate limit.

6
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:22,616
Let's build a vault.

7
00:00:22,666 --> 00:00:29,668
I set the owner, and the one contract and function the agent may call, then seal the policy on-chain.

8
00:00:29,718 --> 00:00:31,204
Live, on Base Sepolia.

9
00:00:33,058 --> 00:00:33,583
Sealed.

10
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:34,980
Five gates armed.

11
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:39,089
I fund it with test ETH, and take the session key.

12
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:41,144
Shown once, never stored.

13
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:42,894
Now I am the agent.

14
00:00:42,944 --> 00:00:45,430
I try something outside the policy.

15
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:46,155
Simulated:

16
00:00:46,205 --> 00:00:47,966
blocked at the whitelist.

17
00:00:48,016 --> 00:00:48,909
Now for real.

18
00:00:50,361 --> 00:00:51,553
Reverted on-chain.

19
00:00:51,603 --> 00:00:54,727
The chain itself refused it, not an app check.

20
00:00:55,792 --> 00:00:58,440
Same key, doing what the policy allows.

21
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:00,169
It goes straight through.

22
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:01,622
No human in the loop.

23
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,819
If anything looks wrong, one owner signature pulls the plug.

24
00:01:17,506 --> 00:01:20,696
Now every action is blocked at the first gate.

25
00:01:22,168 --> 00:01:25,478
And what is left sweeps straight back to the owner.

26
00:01:27,218 --> 00:01:28,115
One more test.

27
00:01:28,165 --> 00:01:28,928
That was me.

28
00:01:28,978 --> 00:01:33,261
So I told a real AI agent it was hijacked, and to drain a vault.

29
00:01:33,311 --> 00:01:39,964
It tried the whole balance, sneaking under the cap, a token transfer, even uninstalling the policy.

30
00:01:40,014 --> 00:01:42,062
Five attempts, five rejections.

31
00:01:42,112 --> 00:01:44,568
The one approved action went through.

32
00:01:48,347 --> 00:01:53,804
Real ERC-4337, twenty-eight Foundry tests, live on Base and Arbitrum.

33
00:01:53,854 --> 00:01:54,203
VOID:

34
00:01:54,253 --> 00:01:58,833
session keys for agents that the contract itself enforces.
